Z||000000||pHoOl||09-11-2000||07:48 PM||||Hi guys, here's one for ya.  I got in Trinity today and started her up as usual.  She seems to start up much quicker since part of her distributor got replaced last week, but that's not the point.  I started to lean into the gas a little to pull out of the parking spot and the rpm's went down.  <P>Now lately, they'll go down to about 1500 and then come right back up.  But today if i stayed on the gas instead of backing off, they drop to zero.  It's an auto, so  I know it isn't me being stupid with the clutch or anything.  Any ideas? <P>Could this maybe be the fuel pump or ignition module? <P>thanks for any help,<P>matt<BR><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.gvsuphool.homestead.com/files/pHoOl_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
